00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:04.780
Beth: All individuals with autism have a
unique set of strengths and abilities and

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.500
to help them reach their full potential
it is important to identify them.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:13.270
Once identified working with these
strengths can be a way of helping improve

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:15.450
their general motivation and development.

00:00:16.219 --> 00:00:19.740
Some individuals with autism will
be very driven by their particular

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:23.160
skills and interests and if
these are utilised appropriately,

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:24.930
they can increase motivation.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.199
let’s look at some examples of
strengths commonly associated with

00:00:29.219 --> 00:00:32.699
autism and especially individuals
that are high functioning.

00:00:33.139 --> 00:00:36.120
- Joe: Specialist knowledge and
a high motivation in topics and

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.639
activities that are of interest.

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:42.140
- Exceptional memory for facts and
figures and the ability to carry

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:45.340
out mathematical tasks mentally
with a high degree of accuracy.

00:00:46.429 --> 00:00:48.569
- An innovative approach to problem solving.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:54.010
- Innate skills in creative arts,
such as Art and Music and use

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:56.089
of memory to enhance this.

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:59.047
- Enthusiasm for favourite interests with a
drive to share this enjoyment with others.

00:00:59.047 --> 00:01:02.504
- Good almost obsessive attention to
detail and ability to follow instructions

00:01:02.504 --> 00:01:04.498
especially when taught correctly.

00:01:04.498 --> 00:01:08.486
- A tendency to be honest and plain talking

00:01:08.486 --> 00:01:14.140
- Ability to see the world from
a different perspective and can

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.420
bring a different insight to things

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:20.340
Beth: By working with and supporting the
individual to bolster their strengths and

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:25.270
abilities, a person with Autism should
be enabled to reach their potential and

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:29.809
focus on what motivates them, and in turn
this should improve their confidence and

00:01:29.809 --> 00:01:32.340
self-worth in all aspects of their life.

